  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements :<br />Statement I : If the Brewster&#39;s angle for the light propagating from air to glass is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math>, then Brewster&#39;s angle for the light propagating from glass to air is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math>.</p><p>Statement II : The Brewster&#39;s angle for the light propagating from glass to air is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></msub></mfenced></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></msub></math> is the refractive index of glass.<br />In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Both Statements I and Statement II are true.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false.",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true.",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0068_9cd445cdf487.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 205px;\" /></p><p>Applying Snell&#39;s law, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mi>sin</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></msub><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></msub><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>When going from glass to air<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>cot</mi><mi>i</mi></math></p><p>Clearly,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;&amp; hence&nbsp;Statement I is true but Statement II is false.</p>"
  }
}